  "The double-positive rate across the campaign (16/437 = 3.7%) exceeds the independence expectation (2.4%) only modestly; this set is NOT established as distinguishable from search noise.",
  "Of 75 cells that passed holdout, only 21.3% stayed positive on confirmation, against a 14.2% marginal rate.",
  "Cells are not independent: adjacent timeframes share signals, and ta_stochastic and ta_williams_r rows appear numerically identical in several cases.",
  "No shifted-label or permutation null has been run against these survivors.",
  "The retrospective confirmation window ends 2026-08-01, so tracking after that date is genuinely unseen data. That is the purpose of this registry."
 ],
 "rules": {
  "long": "fast > slow AND one unconsumed recent bullish regular divergence on the slow oscillator",
  "short": "fast < slow AND one unconsumed recent bearish regular divergence on the slow oscillator",
  "consumption": "each divergence confirmation arms exactly ONE entry and is consumed on the first bar whose fast/slow relation agrees; a live lookback cannot re-open a position every bar",
  "confirmation_timing": "divergence confirms only after the configured right-hand pivot bars complete; events emit on the completed confirmation bar",
  "entry_execution": "open(t+1)"
 },
